-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e89ab6a370cbb37bb6727edcb3faf9c6c4b51ce259816aac38c5ef49fe8f319c","event_uuid":"df9c4bb6-0d0a-4cca-950f-75d462df0711","position":{"commit_sha":"ab57d4accaf02534c470e6a89c11b30834faaf52","position":"1787367495735007001-df9c4bb6-0d0a-4cca-950f-75d462df0711"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"99798d109f14c74c5491ccde89a1e974e19eee8fece7d6182fda7ea38ed49092","event_uuid":"67459812-7b6b-4010-b1d8-7c7cade5baaf","position":{"commit_sha":"1e33d2e8dce32f9704df38e8fd0a172323df4133","position":"1787368592049179082-67459812-7b6b-4010-b1d8-7c7cade5baaf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cf2ccd6829c74de662d8d93bf4e4ced288ddb14343f79b8e9b49f834514c6b99","event_uuid":"1e3a462f-41ae-43cd-8ecf-62eb238d44b3","position":{"commit_sha":"46038fb60ac39b099809bf66e5e688da541fed23","position":"1787369739499216001-1e3a462f-41ae-43cd-8ecf-62eb238d44b3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c6716ae4507cc1d400f963ff52eec0717d66835792062ed90bfc96dade3fd309","event_uuid":"f5e3d917-cc18-493f-89e2-2b6b2c331bda","position":{"commit_sha":"832e3507fd12ad9927e581cfd84d6024d2a30489","position":"1787371155674473001-f5e3d917-cc18-493f-89e2-2b6b2c331bda"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8284c42e37fcd7c50c325e5bf2c1a38d3eb71c5b52c4561959fe1143b144726f","event_uuid":"60468d81-6755-4e6a-9288-951a0fe5527c","position":{"commit_sha":"033c932fbbdd69f1585c8440f790233ad06fa301","position":"1787371171627156001-60468d81-6755-4e6a-9288-951a0fe5527c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Reclassified bug -> task: the concrete defect already landed with 103729e90c; what remains is process/guardrail work\n\nThe concrete convergence defect this ticket documents — a re-derived oracle blind to send-path drift — was fixed in commit `103729e90c` (\"Fit the comment dedup key like the send path\", verified reachable from origin/main): the test now captures the `--body` argument from a real `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` call with only `acli_subprocess._run_acli` stubbed, so the send side of the assertion moves with the send path.\n\nWhat remains in this ticket's acceptance criteria is process/guardrail work — decide and record the rule that convergence tests must capture the external-effect side from the real call site rather than recompute it, and make that rule discoverable/enforceable. That is designed guardrail work with no currently-broken behaviour behind it, i.e. task-shaped, not a defect. Type changed bug -> task; the evidence and ACs are unchanged.","timestamp":1787333929205398001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Mechanical-check evaluation (AC3): decision — do NOT add the lint\n\nProposed check: flag a test that imports the same fit/encode helper the module under test uses on both sides of an equality assertion.\n\nSurvey of the current tree (grep -rln 'fit_outbound|truncate_comment_body|fit_preserving_marker' tests/): **17 test files** import at least one of the shared fit helpers. The set includes tests whose sanctioned job is exactly the flagged shape:\n\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py::test_dc_fit_comment_is_the_send_path_fit — deliberately pins fit_comment byte-identical to the send-path fit by calling both helpers on both sides of an equality.\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py::test_fit_comment_converges_with_sanitize_comment — same sanctioned shape.\n- Direct unit tests of the helpers themselves (comment_limits / AdfCodec.fit_outbound), which necessarily call the helper on both the arrange and assert side.\n\nThe defective shape and the sanctioned shape are syntactically identical: both are 'equality assertion where each side is derived via a shared fit helper'. What distinguishes them is INTENT — whether one side *represents an external effect* (a landed Jira body) rather than the helper's own contract. That property is not recoverable from imports or AST structure, so any implementable version of the check either (a) flags the ~17 legitimate files (unacceptable false-positive cost, and the noise trains authors to suppress it) or (b) is narrowed until it cannot catch the next instance (the two historical instances used *different* compositions — truncate_comment_body vs fit_preserving_marker(...) — so a pattern-list check goes stale exactly like the tests it polices).\n\nDecision: record the rule as authoring guidance instead — landed in examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md §4 ('Convergence tests: capture the external-effect side, never re-derive it', with both instances as the worked example), synced byte-identically to the rebar-debug/rebar-implement/rebar-brainstorm copies (gated by tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py).","timestamp":1787367495735007001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787312432937795001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ca0b3e00-931d-46ca-b620-1508fa070c51","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e339-9709-15fe-419a"},{"link_uuid":"ec0ab0f2-fae2-4d12-9c42-2c488f3691da","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3fce-cccf-d38b-4072"},{"link_uuid":"67459812-7b6b-4010-b1d8-7c7cade5baaf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6eed-1d76-bd16-42f2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA convergence test that RE-DERIVES what the send path does — instead of DRIVING the send path\nand capturing what it produced — measures the helper it named, not the convergence it claims.\nIt stays green when the send path drifts, which is the only failure it exists to catch. This\nhappened twice in the same module:\n\n1. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py` modelled\n   the landed Jira body as `comment_limits.truncate_comment_body(emitted_body)`. When\n   `emersed-specific-mutt` moved the Cloud send path onto `AdfCodec.fit_outbound`, the model\n   went stale and the test kept passing while live convergence was broken (bug\n   `abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey`, 836 unmarked duplicate comments in live Jira).\n2. The first draft of that bug's own fix re-derived the send side as\n   `fit_preserving_marker(_decorate_outbound_comment(body), codec.fit_outbound)` — a copy of\n   the composition under test — and passed Gerrit CI with `Verified +1`. Seeding the exact\n   original mistake back into `add_comment` left it GREEN (8 passed re-derived vs 2 failed\n   captured, recorded in this ticket's history).\n\nThe concrete test defect is already fixed: commit `103729e90c` landed\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py`, whose\n`_send` helper captures the `--body` argument from a real `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` call with\nonly `acli_subprocess._run_acli` stubbed. What remains is guardrail work: nothing in the repo\ntells the next test author which of the two shapes is correct — `make lint`, the complexity\nratchet and code review all passed the re-derived version.\n\n## Approach\n\nRecord the rule in the shared test-design standard — the guidance test authors are already\ndirected to at oracle-design time (`examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md:627` and\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md:214` both point at `test-design.md` in their\nskill directory) — rather than inventing a new document. Add a titled paragraph to\n`examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` §4 \"Trigger the mechanism; assert the contract\"\n(the section that governs what an oracle may assert, and one of the sections that \"apply to\nevery test\" per the scale-ceremony rule, so no section renumbering is needed): in a\nconvergence/agreement test, the side of the assertion that represents an external effect must\nbe CAPTURED from the real call site — drive the production entry point with only the\nirreducible boundary stubbed and capture what it handed the boundary — never RE-DERIVED by\nrecomposing the helpers that call site uses today. Use the two instances above as the compact\nworked example (stale re-derived model vs. the landed captured `--body` oracle). Then sync the\nbyte-identical per-skill copies exactly per `examples/agent-skills/README.md` §\"The shared\ntest-design standard\" (`cp` canonical over `rebar-debug`/`rebar-implement`/`rebar-brainstorm`\ncopies); the existing gating test `tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py` enforces the sync.\n\nFor the mechanical-check AC, evaluate the proposed lint (flag a test that imports the same\nfit/encode helper the module under test uses on both sides of an equality assertion) against\nthe current tree and record the verdict as a comment on this ticket. Default decision: do NOT\nadd it — 17 test files under `tests/` already import\n`fit_outbound`/`truncate_comment_body`/`fit_preserving_marker`, and the legitimate\ncharacterization shape (e.g. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py`\ndeliberately pins `fit_comment` equal to the send-path fit by calling both helpers) is\nsyntactically identical to the defective shape; whether one assertion side \"represents an\nexternal effect\" is intent, not syntax, so the check cannot be written without flagging the\nsanctioned tests. The comment records the survey numbers so the decision is auditable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` — add the capture-don't-re-derive rule +\n  worked example to §4 (canonical copy).\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/test-design.md` — byte-identical sync of the canonical.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/test-design.md` — byte-identical sync.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/test-design.md` — byte-identical sync.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only change — no new testable runtime behavior. The one existing gating test\nthat covers this edit is the copy-sync guard: `pytest tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py`\nmust pass (it fails if any per-skill copy diverges from the canonical file). `make lint` and\n`make typecheck` run as usual.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` §4 states the rule — the external-effect\n      side of a convergence assertion is captured from the real call site, not recomputed\n      from the helpers that call site uses — and names both worked examples from this ticket\n      (the stale `truncate_comment_body` model and the captured `--body` oracle that replaced\n      it). Check: `grep -n \"re-derive\" examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` hits\n      inside §4 and a read of the paragraph confirms both examples.\n- [x] All three consuming skill copies are byte-identical to the canonical file. Check:\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py` passes.\n- [x] The mechanical-check evaluation is recorded as a comment on this ticket: the decision\n      (add / don't add) plus the false-positive evidence (the survey counts of legitimate\n      tests importing the shared fit helpers). Check: `rebar show` on this ticket shows the\n      comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md","reason":"Add the capture-dont-re-derive convergence-test rule with worked examples (canonical copy)."},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/test-design.md","reason":"Byte-identical sync of the canonical standard."},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/test-design.md","reason":"Byte-identical sync of the canonical standard."},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/test-design.md","reason":"Byte-identical sync of the canonical standard."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3fce-cccf-d38b-4072"],["relates_to","6eed-1d76-bd16-42f2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f5e3d917-cc18-493f-89e2-2b6b2c331bda","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4b87-e163-cd9e-43c8","ticket_type":"task","title":"Convergence tests re-derive the send path instead of driving it","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ec0ab0f2-fae2-4d12-9c42-2c488f3691da","1df3b652-a89e-4e3a-a019-2ca87f1b82c8","5248a38f-311d-4fc9-bc6b-662e73bcd0f1","78a54336-9135-49e9-af4d-501a67cd5542","de61897f-f112-435c-ac7c-a1e1ffb1edb7","a6d2a15f-3d60-4d49-b826-6e6aa4bccafd","25d8bb0d-462b-45c4-b9d7-a8128e75be14","49c51da7-2770-4698-ad84-32ab7c2023c3","df9c4bb6-0d0a-4cca-950f-75d462df0711","67459812-7b6b-4010-b1d8-7c7cade5baaf","1e3a462f-41ae-43cd-8ecf-62eb238d44b3","f5e3d917-cc18-493f-89e2-2b6b2c331bda","60468d81-6755-4e6a-9288-951a0fe5527c"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787378788544372615,"uuid":"06e9e4f5-2177-4e8a-a236-a68b49549bd9"}